From 578752f660e68c66412d4d0c08dccfc84c6724dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: syang-genai <191082996+syang-genai@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:08:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] eplb: aggregate the expert-count window by logical expert at
 record time

The expert-count window stored raw per-local-physical-slot counts and
decoded every entry with the physical_to_logical_map that is current at
rearrangement time. Each rearrangement re-keys the physical slots, so
entries recorded under an earlier placement were attributed to whichever
logical expert now occupies the slot.

In interval mode this is masked because window_size <= interval, so the
ring is fully overwritten between rearrangements. With
DEEPINFER_REARRANGE_AFTER_PREFILL_IN_NORMAL_ENGINE=1 a rearrangement is
forced after every prefill step, which under continuous batching happens
far more often than window_size decode steps; most of the window then
holds counts recorded under one or more dead placements, and
rebalance_experts_global optimizes a scrambled load distribution. The
rank_balance / logical_balance metrics are derived from the same counts,
so the logs do not reveal it.

Record the window as [window_size, num_moe_layers, num_logical_experts]
by scatter-adding each step's slot counts with the placement that is
current when the step is recorded. _rearrange_experts then only has to
all-reduce the window. The shape handed to rebalance_experts_global and
to the metrics logging is unchanged.

Add CPU-only tests that drive the recording path directly and check that
an entry recorded before a placement change keeps its original
attribution, that ring wrap replaces rather than accumulates, and that
the rank slice follows the rank.
